WEBVTT

00:00:17.410 --> 00:00:18.660
Sarasa.

00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:23.710
I have superpowers and
can read your mind right now.

00:00:23.710 --> 00:00:25.090
Can I say something to help you?

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:29.380
Even if you can't walk down
the kabuki <i>hanamichi </i>anymore...

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:33.850
...we can walk down
the Kouka silver bridge.

00:00:35.390 --> 00:00:36.510
How's that sound?

00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:39.480
Great!

00:02:11.150 --> 00:02:14.280
The students at the Kouka School
of Musical and Theatrical Arts

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:17.320
return to campus, refreshed from
their summer vacation,

00:02:17.320 --> 00:02:21.870
and began to ready themselves
for a new semester.

00:02:21.870 --> 00:02:24.000
It's so much hotter down here!

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:25.960
You guys went up north to Hokkaido, right?

00:02:25.960 --> 00:02:28.340
Yeah, summers there are super cool.

00:02:28.340 --> 00:02:31.170
I saw two of the Spring Troupe's shows!

00:02:31.170 --> 00:02:35.470
I have to say, Ryuu Asahina's
Chiaki Raku was transcendent!

00:02:36.510 --> 00:02:38.640
Whoa, Hoshino-<i>san</i>!

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:42.430
You cut your hair!

00:02:42.430 --> 00:02:44.180
It was hot long.

00:02:44.180 --> 00:02:45.350
Oh, wow!

00:02:45.350 --> 00:02:48.360
You've got such great hair,
so of course it'd look good short!

00:02:48.360 --> 00:02:53.740
I <i>do </i>want to be an <i>otoko-yaku</i>,
so I figured now's the time to cut it.

00:02:53.740 --> 00:02:56.780
You're so cool! You look so handsome!

00:02:56.780 --> 00:02:59.910
C'mon, guys, literally everyone
cuts their hair!

00:02:59.910 --> 00:03:00.950
She's embarrassed.

00:03:00.950 --> 00:03:02.790
Kaoru's embarrassed.

00:03:02.790 --> 00:03:04.200
You're totally embarrassed!

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:08.790
Whatever! What the hell is
wrong with you and Naracchi?!

00:03:08.790 --> 00:03:12.380
I keep telling you to
start acting like pros!

00:03:12.380 --> 00:03:16.050
Pros don't let themselves
get suntanned like that!

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:19.050
What kind of reaction is that?!

00:03:19.050 --> 00:03:22.510
And don't act like you're
not in trouble, too, Naracchi!

00:03:22.510 --> 00:03:28.480
I was just having so much fun,
I didn't realize I was getting tan.

00:03:28.480 --> 00:03:34.230
That doesn't matter! Fine Kouka ladies
do <i>not </i>let themselves get a tan!

00:03:35.740 --> 00:03:37.360
Eek.

00:03:37.360 --> 00:03:39.910
Kaoru <i>does </i>go all-out.

00:03:44.240 --> 00:03:47.160
Why does Hoshino always
walk around with an umbrella?

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:48.830
Who knows?

00:03:48.830 --> 00:03:50.920
A teacher told her to lose the umbrella,

00:03:50.920 --> 00:03:54.840
but she argued there's
no school rule against them!

00:03:54.840 --> 00:03:59.130
Apparently she wants to be an actress or
something? So she doesn't want to get tan.

00:04:02.760 --> 00:04:06.930
So then I posted it!

00:04:06.930 --> 00:04:08.850
You <i>didn't</i>!

00:04:10.440 --> 00:04:15.400
Whoa, look over there.
He's on our baseball team.

00:04:15.400 --> 00:04:16.230
Huh?

00:04:16.230 --> 00:04:19.950
Y'know, he's related to
that hot major leaguer.

00:04:20.950 --> 00:04:24.660
Really? He's like, not even hot though.

00:04:24.660 --> 00:04:28.370
You think we'll finally
make it to Koshien this year?

00:04:29.160 --> 00:04:32.080
Ugh, look at her!

00:04:32.080 --> 00:04:35.500
A school uniform <i>and </i>an umbrella?
Who does she think she is?

00:04:35.500 --> 00:04:38.260
Oh, she went to my middle school.

00:04:38.260 --> 00:04:41.260
Apparently she wants to go to
the Kouka theater school,

00:04:41.260 --> 00:04:43.970
but she still hasn't gotten in yet.

00:04:54.940 --> 00:04:58.190
We live near the sea.

00:04:58.190 --> 00:05:01.740
The sun shines bright, especially during
these hot summer months.

00:05:01.740 --> 00:05:04.070
I can do what I can
to keep from getting tan,

00:05:04.070 --> 00:05:07.080
but there's not much I can do
about the heat.

00:05:12.420 --> 00:05:15.090
I'm so glad you're
feeling better, Mari-<i>chan</i>!

00:05:15.090 --> 00:05:18.210
I was so scared when I heard
you were in the hospital!

00:05:19.210 --> 00:05:22.010
Come on in.

00:05:22.010 --> 00:05:24.510
How are you feeling, Grandma?

00:05:24.510 --> 00:05:28.350
Oh, Kaoru-<i>chan</i>! How nice of you to visit!

00:05:28.350 --> 00:05:33.350
My grandmother was a top <i>musume-yaku</i>
of the Kouka Acting Troupe.

00:05:33.350 --> 00:05:36.230
They called her
"Spring's Lovely Snow White."

00:05:36.230 --> 00:05:39.650
Even now, she's still surrounded by fans.

00:05:39.650 --> 00:05:42.360
My goodness, is this her?

00:05:42.360 --> 00:05:43.570
Yes, my granddaughter.

00:05:43.570 --> 00:05:46.200
Oh, my! It's nice to meet you!

00:05:46.200 --> 00:05:48.790
She's a senior in high school now.

00:05:48.790 --> 00:05:50.830
Is she? Then that means...

00:05:50.830 --> 00:05:56.000
She must be breaking from tradition and
won't be joining the Kouka troupe, then?

00:05:56.000 --> 00:06:01.050
This is her last year to apply, so she's
giving it all she's got right now.

00:06:01.050 --> 00:06:03.050
My, is that right!

00:06:03.050 --> 00:06:06.550
We're rooting for you, hon! Break a leg!

00:06:08.390 --> 00:06:11.680
Your kidney stone surgery
must have been so scary.

00:06:11.680 --> 00:06:15.560
Though with how you sparkle,
I'm sure they pulled out a diamond!

00:06:15.560 --> 00:06:20.360
Everyone must be so disappointed.
After all, I hardly look the part.

00:06:22.070 --> 00:06:23.990
Semester's finally over!

00:06:23.990 --> 00:06:26.160
Let's hit karaoke on the way home!

00:06:26.160 --> 00:06:27.910
I'm going on a date with my boyfriend.

00:06:27.910 --> 00:06:28.950
What are you up to, Kaoru?

00:06:28.950 --> 00:06:31.290
I've got lessons every day from now on.

00:06:31.290 --> 00:06:32.330
Wait, really?

00:06:32.330 --> 00:06:34.920
Kaoru's so weird.

00:06:35.830 --> 00:06:38.790
I want to be an <i>otoko-yaku</i>!

00:06:41.630 --> 00:06:44.720
A cool, handsome actress
who plays male roles!

00:06:52.390 --> 00:06:54.390
Sorry, I was in the middle of class.

00:06:54.390 --> 00:06:57.900
Could you stop by the hospital
on your way home?

00:06:57.900 --> 00:07:00.480
Grandma mentioned a book
she wanted us to pick up for her.

00:07:00.480 --> 00:07:02.110
Yeah, sure.

00:07:02.110 --> 00:07:03.990
Okay, thanks!

00:07:15.290 --> 00:07:18.080
H-Hey, uh.

00:07:19.960 --> 00:07:24.670
I heard some girls the other day say you
were trying out for some acting troupe.

00:07:24.670 --> 00:07:27.840
And, uh, my grandma's
a big fan of that troupe,

00:07:27.840 --> 00:07:30.890
so she told me to ask you some questions.

00:07:30.890 --> 00:07:32.430
Like what?

00:07:32.430 --> 00:07:34.600
Like... what's your name?

00:07:35.480 --> 00:07:39.310
Ugh, what am I even saying...

00:07:39.310 --> 00:07:41.190
Excuse me!

00:07:41.190 --> 00:07:43.820
Are you Tsuji-<i>san </i>from South High?

00:07:43.820 --> 00:07:45.900
Uh, yeah?

00:07:45.900 --> 00:07:48.660
Good luck in the Koshien prelims.

00:07:48.660 --> 00:07:54.740
Also, could you give this
to your brother Kaito?!

00:07:56.620 --> 00:07:59.790
I really, really like him.

00:07:59.790 --> 00:08:03.590
Whenever I feel down, I just watch
him play, and it makes me feel better.

00:08:03.590 --> 00:08:05.630
I know he's headed off
to the major leagues,

00:08:05.630 --> 00:08:08.340
and he's engaged
to that model, Seira-<i>chan</i>,

00:08:08.340 --> 00:08:11.300
but I'd really appreciate it
if you'd give him my letter!

00:08:13.680 --> 00:08:15.930
I don't want any part in that.

00:08:15.930 --> 00:08:21.060
I'm not my brother's keeper.

00:08:21.060 --> 00:08:21.810
B-But--

00:08:21.810 --> 00:08:24.610
The school <i>and </i>my brother
don't want people doing this.

00:08:27.530 --> 00:08:28.950
I'm sorry!

00:08:31.110 --> 00:08:32.740
You okay?

00:08:34.410 --> 00:08:36.330
Please don't cry.

00:08:38.080 --> 00:08:39.540
Hoshino.

00:08:40.580 --> 00:08:45.460
That's my name.
Kaoru Hoshino. What's yours?

00:08:46.630 --> 00:08:48.010
Rikuto Tsuji.

00:08:52.180 --> 00:08:54.220
The Kouka School of
Musical and Theatrical Arts?

00:08:54.220 --> 00:08:55.350
Yep.

00:08:55.350 --> 00:08:56.970
What do they teach you there?

00:08:56.970 --> 00:09:00.060
Everything from proper manners
to singing and ballet.

00:09:00.060 --> 00:09:02.690
We do a <i>lot </i>of physical training.

00:09:02.690 --> 00:09:03.520
Damn!

00:09:03.520 --> 00:09:07.440
Right? I gotta be able to lift
those <i>musume-yaku </i>girls!

00:09:07.440 --> 00:09:08.940
<i>Musume </i>what?

00:09:08.940 --> 00:09:13.530
The troupe's all-female, so they sort
actresses into male or female roles.

00:09:14.870 --> 00:09:17.490
Are you gonna have to wear a moustache?

00:09:17.490 --> 00:09:21.500
Yeah! The guys in my class
make fun of that all the time.

00:09:21.500 --> 00:09:25.380
Oh, I didn't mean to
make fun of it! I was just surprised.

00:09:29.880 --> 00:09:33.130
I've seen your brother on TV a few times.

00:09:34.510 --> 00:09:38.680
Oh, yeah. Yeah, figures.

00:09:38.680 --> 00:09:40.230
That's not what I meant.

00:09:40.230 --> 00:09:44.600
My mom and grandma
were both in the Kouka troupe,

00:09:44.600 --> 00:09:48.110
and my grandma was pretty famous.

00:09:48.110 --> 00:09:51.570
I was just thinking how
we have that in common.

00:09:59.450 --> 00:10:01.620
Rikuto's on the South High
Varsity Baseball Team,

00:10:01.620 --> 00:10:05.670
and every year, they make it to
at least the Koshien prelim finals.

00:10:05.670 --> 00:10:10.090
But Rikuto usually ends up
warming the bench.

00:10:10.090 --> 00:10:12.470
Tsuji's gotten a hell of
a lot better all of the sudden.

00:10:12.470 --> 00:10:16.340
He's got the skill, that's for sure.

00:10:16.340 --> 00:10:20.060
He just gets into his head too much.

00:10:20.060 --> 00:10:22.680
Hey, guys, come eat!

00:10:25.350 --> 00:10:28.690
Here! I made this one for you.

00:10:28.690 --> 00:10:29.900
Thanks.

00:10:29.900 --> 00:10:33.990
We're graduating this year, so you better
make it to Koshien this time!

00:10:33.990 --> 00:10:37.070
Good point. Not like I'll
get to play, though.

00:10:37.070 --> 00:10:42.290
Oh, c'mon! Your brother's going to
the major leagues! You can do it!

00:10:46.080 --> 00:10:48.750
I never get bothered when
people try to compare me to them!

00:10:48.750 --> 00:10:52.130
Just 'cause we're related doesn't mean
we're the same! I'm me!

00:10:52.130 --> 00:10:53.420
Wow.

00:10:53.420 --> 00:10:54.630
You're so strong.

00:10:56.550 --> 00:10:59.430
You have a hard time
expressing yourself when you sing.

00:10:59.430 --> 00:11:03.140
Give it more feeling and
enunciate those syllables.

00:11:03.140 --> 00:11:04.060
Yes, ma'am.

00:11:04.060 --> 00:11:06.520
Don't worry! You'll be a great singer.

00:11:06.520 --> 00:11:09.650
Your mother and grandmother
were both great singers.

00:11:13.860 --> 00:11:16.240
I'm me.

00:11:16.240 --> 00:11:18.070
That's what I keep telling myself.

00:11:22.620 --> 00:11:28.960
♬ Falling from the sky ♬

00:11:28.960 --> 00:11:34.300
♬ Like white snow, but warm, ♬

00:11:34.300 --> 00:11:40.680
♬ Like a spring fairy ♬

00:11:40.680 --> 00:11:45.350
♬ Fluttering down ♬

00:11:51.020 --> 00:11:54.360
When are you visiting your grandma next?

00:11:58.950 --> 00:11:59.950
Huh?

00:12:00.870 --> 00:12:03.620
The sun's really bright today.

00:12:03.620 --> 00:12:07.460
Oh, yeah, you've gotta
watch out for that, huh.

00:12:10.000 --> 00:12:13.800
I'm super tan, like Othello.

00:12:15.170 --> 00:12:17.420
In the center of the Kouka stage,

00:12:17.420 --> 00:12:20.470
there's this part of the apron
called the silver bridge.

00:12:20.470 --> 00:12:24.100
Only a few stars get to walk across it.

00:12:24.100 --> 00:12:25.890
The big stars, huh?

00:12:25.890 --> 00:12:29.850
I'm gonna be a top <i>otoko-yaku</i>
and walk across that silver bridge.

00:12:32.270 --> 00:12:36.780
You know those people who <i>say </i>"I'm getting
in!" when there's no guarantee they will,

00:12:36.780 --> 00:12:38.450
then end up getting in?

00:12:38.450 --> 00:12:39.490
Yeah?

00:12:39.490 --> 00:12:43.030
I'll be honest, I wish I had their guts.

00:12:43.030 --> 00:12:48.660
I could never say that. I know better than
anyone just how hard it is to get in.

00:12:51.210 --> 00:12:53.750
When are you going to
see your grandma again?

00:12:55.340 --> 00:12:58.420
You sure have been coming to see me a lot!

00:12:58.420 --> 00:13:00.880
Y-You think so?

00:13:03.050 --> 00:13:05.060
How many guys are on a baseball team?

00:13:05.060 --> 00:13:08.310
Nine. You hear the English number
used a lot, right?

00:13:08.310 --> 00:13:10.480
I don't know anything about baseball.

00:13:10.480 --> 00:13:12.730
You <i>do </i>spend all your time taking lessons.

00:13:16.520 --> 00:13:19.820
I can't come to watch,
but I hope you guys win.

00:13:25.410 --> 00:13:30.250
I'll have to wear more manly fashions
when I get into the troupe,

00:13:30.250 --> 00:13:34.130
so I'm wearing all the skirts
I can right now.

00:13:35.000 --> 00:13:37.460
Y'know, Hoshino-<i>san</i>,
I bet that even with a moustache,

00:13:37.460 --> 00:13:39.340
you'd <i>still </i>look pretty.

00:13:40.670 --> 00:13:42.380
What the hell?

00:13:42.380 --> 00:13:44.260
Oh my God. Oh my God.

00:13:44.260 --> 00:13:46.720
He didn't. Oh, geez.

00:13:49.680 --> 00:13:54.190
I've <i>never </i>gotten called pretty by a boy.

00:14:01.780 --> 00:14:05.410
C'mere, girls! We've got
a veteran joining us today!

00:14:05.410 --> 00:14:09.910
Ta-dah! Here's an admittee
from our dance school,

00:14:09.910 --> 00:14:12.870
second-year Kouka student Yamagishi-<i>san</i>!

00:14:12.870 --> 00:14:16.750
She'll be using our studio to practice
over her summer break.

00:14:16.750 --> 00:14:19.170
Thank you for having me!

00:14:19.170 --> 00:14:20.960
Kaoru-<i>chan</i>!

00:14:23.260 --> 00:14:27.890
I'm so glad you're still
trying to get into Kouka!

00:14:27.890 --> 00:14:30.310
Yeah, this year's my last chance.

00:14:30.310 --> 00:14:34.770
Oh, wow. Let me know
if I can help you at all!

00:14:34.770 --> 00:14:39.650
You helped me a lot when
I was trying to get in, after all!

00:14:42.400 --> 00:14:45.160
Hey, what's up with Yamagishi-<i>san</i>?

00:14:45.160 --> 00:14:47.280
Yeah, she's kind of a ditz.

00:14:47.280 --> 00:14:50.450
She always went on and on about how
she was gonna be the 'next top star.'

00:14:50.450 --> 00:14:52.870
She was good friends with Kaoru,

00:14:52.870 --> 00:14:56.630
but then she got in right after
ninth grade, on her first try!

00:14:56.630 --> 00:15:00.710
Wow. And Hoshino-<i>san</i>'s
on her fourth try now.

00:15:00.710 --> 00:15:03.260
Guess having connections
doesn't help you get in.

00:15:03.260 --> 00:15:05.430
You've gotta have the talent.

00:15:15.480 --> 00:15:18.310
My, you're here again!

00:15:18.310 --> 00:15:19.650
Am I coming too often?

00:15:19.650 --> 00:15:25.200
Not at all. I love when
you come to visit me, Kaoru-<i>chan</i>.

00:15:25.200 --> 00:15:27.320
I'll be out of the hospital soon, anyway.

00:15:29.490 --> 00:15:31.370
How are your lessons going?

00:15:31.370 --> 00:15:35.000
Good. I'll be doing daily lessons
for all eight weeks of break.

00:15:35.000 --> 00:15:38.710
My, seven days a week?

00:15:38.710 --> 00:15:43.340
It's wonderful how you young ones
can work so hard and still shine bright.

00:15:44.760 --> 00:15:48.180
But I worry about you.

00:15:48.180 --> 00:15:51.550
You're such a sweet girl. I don't want you
to push yourself too hard.

00:15:52.810 --> 00:15:55.230
If there's something else
you'd like to do,

00:15:55.230 --> 00:15:58.060
you're welcome to do that instead.

00:15:59.310 --> 00:16:01.650
If there's another life
you'd like to live,

00:16:01.650 --> 00:16:04.820
you can always start
down a different path.

00:16:06.150 --> 00:16:07.240
I know.

00:16:16.580 --> 00:16:17.910
You look normal.

00:16:17.910 --> 00:16:19.120
Normal?

00:16:19.120 --> 00:16:21.750
I mean, you're not
covering up or anything.

00:16:21.750 --> 00:16:23.670
Well, the sun's not out.

00:16:23.670 --> 00:16:27.380
This is the first time we've hung out
somewhere other than the bus stop.

00:16:27.380 --> 00:16:29.720
You look good in your yukata.

00:16:29.720 --> 00:16:31.220
C'mon, big bro!

00:16:31.220 --> 00:16:32.100
Hold on!

00:16:32.100 --> 00:16:34.180
We're gonna miss it!

00:16:35.220 --> 00:16:36.430
Wanna walk?

00:16:36.430 --> 00:16:37.850
Yeah.

00:16:37.850 --> 00:16:41.230
Hungry? We've got piping hot <i>okonomiyaki</i>!

00:16:43.900 --> 00:16:46.150
So you're winning all your games!

00:16:46.150 --> 00:16:48.320
Oh, yeah.

00:16:48.320 --> 00:16:50.320
You've won four now?

00:16:50.320 --> 00:16:51.280
Yeah.

00:16:55.870 --> 00:16:57.910
Wow.

00:16:57.910 --> 00:17:00.830
And it's cool that you're hanging out
instead of practicing right now?

00:17:00.830 --> 00:17:01.830
Yeah.

00:17:05.710 --> 00:17:08.260
Hey, what's got you so down?

00:17:11.090 --> 00:17:14.100
I've been doing really well recently,

00:17:14.100 --> 00:17:17.810
but I still haven't gotten a chance
to play in any games.

00:17:17.810 --> 00:17:21.560
Makes me wonder, what's the point
in trying so hard at baseball?

00:17:21.560 --> 00:17:25.150
I grew up playing baseball
with my older brother.

00:17:25.150 --> 00:17:29.780
And since my brother's so talented,
everyone expects me to be good at it, too.

00:17:29.780 --> 00:17:32.530
I figured I had to live up
to those expectations,

00:17:32.530 --> 00:17:35.240
so I joined the baseball team
without a second thought.

00:17:35.240 --> 00:17:39.620
But I keep wondering if I'm wasting
my time forcing myself to do all this.

00:17:40.620 --> 00:17:43.630
I bet you feel that way
all the time, too, huh?

00:17:50.760 --> 00:17:53.760
Why does everyone always assume that?

00:17:53.760 --> 00:17:56.970
I don't. I never do.

00:17:56.970 --> 00:18:02.270
Sure, the pressure gets to me sometimes,
but this is something I <i>want </i>to do!

00:18:02.270 --> 00:18:04.850
I've <i>never </i>forced myself to do this,
not for a second!

00:18:04.850 --> 00:18:08.940
This is the path I chose! I <i>want </i>this!

00:18:08.940 --> 00:18:11.400
And I'm not giving up until the very end!

00:18:11.400 --> 00:18:15.490
I'll do whatever it takes
to get into the Kouka School!

00:18:16.990 --> 00:18:18.240
I-I'm sorry, I--

00:18:18.240 --> 00:18:20.080
Don't assume I'm like you.

00:18:20.080 --> 00:18:21.120
Bye.

00:18:25.000 --> 00:18:27.340
I'm so stupid.

00:18:27.340 --> 00:18:32.050
For a split second, I felt jealous
of the typical high school girl's life.

00:18:32.050 --> 00:18:36.510
Going to karaoke,
going on dates, holding hands.

00:18:36.510 --> 00:18:40.310
Having a boy worry about me
and try to cheer me up.

00:18:48.730 --> 00:18:56.110
♬ Falling from the sky ♬

00:18:56.110 --> 00:19:01.750
♬ Like white snow, but warm, ♬

00:19:01.750 --> 00:19:07.960
♬ Like a spring fairy ♬

00:19:07.960 --> 00:19:13.380
♬ Fluttering down ♬

00:19:13.380 --> 00:19:19.100
♬ Ah, the Kouka cherry blossoms ♬

00:19:19.100 --> 00:19:24.600
♬ Falling upon the earth,
becoming one with the ground, ♬

00:19:24.600 --> 00:19:30.230
♬ to become new life, and go to you ♬

00:19:27.770 --> 00:19:30.230
I'm going to make it.

00:19:30.230 --> 00:19:36.660
♬ Now, they flutter and dance ♬

00:19:36.660 --> 00:19:38.410
I swear...

00:19:38.410 --> 00:19:39.910
I swear I will!

00:19:50.250 --> 00:19:54.670
It's between South High and Hama-Dai
for the finals this year again, eh?

00:19:54.670 --> 00:19:58.260
South High's down by one in the ninth.

00:19:58.260 --> 00:20:00.550
Think they're gonna lose
the final again this year?

00:20:00.550 --> 00:20:04.220
They still got
the bottom of the ninth...

00:20:00.550 --> 00:20:04.220
Pinch hitting for
Number 9's Shimada-<i>kun</i>,

00:20:04.220 --> 00:20:09.020
Tsuji-<i>kun</i>, Number 11!

00:20:10.520 --> 00:20:13.650
Focus! Focus!

00:20:15.360 --> 00:20:18.320
C'mon, Tsuji!

00:20:18.320 --> 00:20:21.530
You can do it! Hit it out of the park!

00:20:36.420 --> 00:20:39.760
Hey, kid! We're missing everything!

00:20:42.510 --> 00:20:44.720
It's outta here!

00:20:44.720 --> 00:20:47.020
Did they win?

00:20:44.720 --> 00:20:47.020
That home run clinches the win!

00:20:47.020 --> 00:20:48.850
Yeah, they won! They won!

00:20:47.020 --> 00:20:48.850
What a way to end a game!

00:20:48.850 --> 00:20:50.560
Whoa, are those tears?

00:20:50.560 --> 00:20:53.770
--Aww, you're cryin' tears of joy!
--South High advances to Koshien!

00:20:54.610 --> 00:20:59.570
South High went to Koshien but
was eliminated after their first game.

00:20:55.350 --> 00:20:57.610
"Koshien Stadium"

00:20:59.570 --> 00:21:02.820
My grandma was discharged
from the hospital,

00:21:02.820 --> 00:21:05.580
and I never went to that bus stop again.

00:21:05.580 --> 00:21:07.330
And now...

00:21:09.080 --> 00:21:12.710
Hey, Sarasa? Could you <i>not</i>
make gross noises?

00:21:12.710 --> 00:21:15.840
You're from Kanagawa, right, Hoshino-<i>san</i>?

00:21:15.840 --> 00:21:20.550
Did you hear about this?
It's getting <i>tons </i>of RTs right now!

00:21:20.550 --> 00:21:26.260
Someone put this letter up
at this bus stop by the sea!

00:21:27.890 --> 00:21:32.480
Please leave this note up for this summer.

00:21:32.480 --> 00:21:37.360
To K: I'm still playing baseball.

00:21:37.360 --> 00:21:39.190
Thank you for everything.

00:21:39.190 --> 00:21:43.280
Nobody knows if it's for a boy or a girl,
or how old they are!

00:21:43.280 --> 00:21:45.950
Isn't that romantic, though?!

00:21:47.290 --> 00:21:48.660
Yeah.

00:21:51.410 --> 00:21:55.960
One day, when I walk across
that silver bridge,

00:21:55.960 --> 00:21:59.050
and you're still playing baseball,

00:21:59.050 --> 00:22:03.390
maybe I'll save you
a primo seat in the SS section.

00:22:05.640 --> 00:22:07.760
Maybe I'll even tell you...

00:22:09.140 --> 00:22:10.980
...that I was in love with you.
